  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nWhen constructing a Complement Docker image for Synapse, we generate a server certificate which contains only a Common Name but no Subject Alternative Name (SAN). Dendrite [doesn't like this](https://golang.google.cn/doc/go1.15#commonname), so refuses to communicate with such a Synapse.\r\n\r\nI encountered this problem because I'm fiddling with trying to extend Complement to support spinning up federations composed of multiple different HS implementations. Synapse <-> Synapse and Dendrite <-> Dendrite work fine, but Synapse <-> Dendrite configurations currently fail to communicate due to this.\r\n\r\nSo to solve this, we need to include a SAN in there. Generating a certificate with SAN using `openssl` is [a bit fiddly](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/6194236/openssl-certificate-version-3-with-subject-alternative-name) but doable, though it looks to be impossible to achieve using just the command-line arguments, so we'd need to bundle an `openssl` config file. Another option would be to generate the server certificate using something other than the `openssl` utility, e.g. using Python's `cryptography` package.\r\n",
